// JVM bytecode - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# JVM class file. The magic is CAFEBABE, then the minor
# and major version, then the constant pool -- whose first
# entry is the UTF-8 string "Hello World!".
CA FE BA BE 00 00 00 34 00 0B
0C 00 0B 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21
